  "Id": 2466,
  "Title": "ISMC Convocation 2014 celebrated",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations convocation held in London.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>The Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations held a convocation ceremony in London, where 13 graduates received their MA in Muslim Cultures.<br/></p><p><p>The Chief Guest was Professor Gudrun Krämer, Professor and Chair of Islamic Studies at Freie Universität Berlin.<br/></p></p><p>ISMC faculty selected two dissertations as the best amongst those submitted by the graduating class. Sana Iqbal, received the joint award for her dissertation titled Swahili Women and their Evolving Agency in the Social Space of Zanzibar. Sana Tajuddin received the award for her dissertation on Exploring the Experience of Confluences: Religious Identities and Sacred Spaces: A Case Study on the Shrine of Shams Sabzwari of Multan, Pakistan.<br/></p><p>The ceremony, held at the Royal College of Surgeons of England, was attended by approximately 100 guests including members of the University's Board of Trustees, ISMC faculty and staff, students' families, as well as friends of the Institute. <br/></p>",
